    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Stunning three bedroom mid terrace brick facade home with a mature back garden ideally located in a quiet cul-de-sac.\r\n\r\nThis charming property features an attractive brick façade with a stained glass front door. The interior of the property enjoys a reverse floor plan with the living accommodation and kitchen upstairs and the bedrooms downstairs. The light filled south east facing living space boasts solid wooden floors, a built in solid fuel stove, alcove & staircase shelving, ornate coving and an exposed brickwork feature wall. The solid flooring continues to the open plan kitchen & dining area with two windows, ornate coving, splashback tiling and plenty of counter & cupboard space. The attic is accessed via a Stira in the kitchen. Downstairs consists of three bedrooms and a bathroom. The first bedroom has solid floors and space for a home office. The second bedroom has laminate floors, fitted wardrobes and ornate coving. The third bedroom is positioned at the rear of the property and comes with solid floors, built in shelving and ornate coving. Double doors open to a recently refurbished fully tiled bathroom with an electric shower and a towel radiator. A chequered tiled hallway leads to the amazing garden which is approx. fifteen metres in length and is the perfect place to relax & entertain on those long summer evenings. The gardens boasts a decked patio, mature trees and a storage shed with utilities. This superb property was refurbished & partially rewired in 2020 and also benefits from three on street parking permits.\r\n\r\nThomas Davis Street West is a quiet cul-de-sac ideally located in Inchicore with plenty of amenities close by such as shops, cafes, restaurants and bars. The LUAS makes the city centre easily accessible, and the Grand Canal makes for a lovely stroll. The Phoenix Park, Memorial Gardens and Royal Hospital all provide excellent leisure facilities. The new children's hospital at St. James's is also within walking distance.\r\n\r\nFeatures:\r\nYear of construction 1911\r\nReverse floor plan\r\nBrick façade\r\n3 parking permits\r\nLarge mature garden\r\nSolid fuel stove\r\nWooden floors\r\nOpen plan kitchen & dining\r\nFeature wall with exposed brickwork\r\nRefurbished & partially rewired - 2020"
      },
